Q: Find exact dimensions of characters A: <p>Use the JavaScript Canvas API. Standard HTML elements always include invisible vertical padding. The Canvas measureText() method measures only the visible pixels of the character.</p>
<p>Visual Height = actualBoundingBoxAscent (top of letter) + actualBoundingBoxDescent (bottom of letter).</p>
<p>Use this function to calculate the height of every character, then use that value to set the specific height or margin of the container for that letter in your vertical layout.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function getExactHeight(text, size, font) {
  const ctx = document.createElement('canvas').getContext('2d');
  ctx.font = `${size}px ${font}`;

  const metrics = ctx.measureText(text);

  return metrics.actualBoundingBoxAscent + metrics.actualBoundingBoxDescent;
}

text.oninput();</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;label&gt;Font:
 &lt;input id="font" value="Arial" oninput="text.oninput()"&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;label&gt;Size:
 &lt;input id="sizepx" value="20" oninput="text.oninput()" type="number"&gt;px&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
&lt;label&gt;Text:
 &lt;input id="text" value="x" oninput="
 var result = getExactHeight(value,sizepx.value,font.value);
 out.value = result;
 samp.textContent = value;
 samp.style.fontFamily = font.value;
 samp.style.fontSize = sizepx.value + 'px';
 mark.style.height = result + 'px';"&gt;&lt;/label&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
Sample ~ visual height:
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span id="samp"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
~
&lt;mark id="mark" style="display: inline-block; width: 10px; background: canvastext;"&gt;&lt;/mark&gt;
&lt;br&gt;Height pixels: &lt;output id="out"&gt;&lt;/output&gt;</code></pre>
